# Tamkeen

Tamkeen is a platform that helps people with visual, auditory, or physical disabilities use websites independently, including government and other service websites, through an accessibility ("enablement") layer matched to the user's disability type.

> **Status:** Draft. The product requirements are written and the project is in the planning phase. No code yet.

## The problem

Most websites are not built for people with disabilities. Navigation is slow, error-prone, or impossible without help, so many users cannot complete tasks on their own. Fixing every site individually is slow and costly.

## How it works

1. The user registers or logs in with email and password.
2. The user selects a disability type: **visual**, **auditory**, or **physical**.
3. The user chooses a supported website from a curated list.
4. Tamkeen opens the website with the matching accessibility features active.

| Disability type | Example features |
|---|---|
| Visual | Screen-reader-friendly structure, text scaling up to 200%, high contrast, visible focus |
| Auditory | Captions or transcripts, visual alerts instead of audio cues |
| Physical | Full keyboard navigation, large click targets (44x44 px), extended timeouts |

## Goals

- Conform to WCAG 2.2 Level AA on all Tamkeen-owned pages.
- Load a target website with the layer active in under 10 seconds (p95).
- Reach at least 80% task completion in usability testing for each disability type.

## Not in v1

Native mobile app, admin panel and reporting, analytics, cognitive disability support, AI features, and third-party integrations.

